--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE READ END-TO-END (the specification)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
InfoTile.tsx is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL LEAF (32 lines). Props:
  icon: React.ElementType | label: string | value: string|number|boolean
  color?: string (default 'text-[var(--text-primary)]') | sub?: string
Logic   : const display = typeof value === 'boolean' ? (value ? 'Yes' : 'No') : value
Layout  : GlassPanel(p-4 overflow-hidden)
            > row(flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--text-muted)] text-xs mb-1.5 min-w-0):
                Icon(h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0) + span(truncate){label}
            > p(text-lg font-semibold truncate, color, title=String(display)){display}
            > sub && p(text-[10px] text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-0.5){sub}
It fetches NOTHING. There are NO hooks, NO async, NO loading/error/stale/offline branches in
the source. The only conditional render branches are: (a) boolean value -> "Yes"/"No";
(b) non-boolean value rendered verbatim; (c) optional sub line; (d) value tint via `color`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web -> native; ADR-002 shared SwiftUI source, ADR-009 tokens)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources: NONE (pure presentational). The prompt's "Data sources (from web source)"
  is "(none — pure presentational component)". Therefore there is no P1/S8 state-holder to
  bind and NO HTTP anywhere — matching the source exactly (covenant 2: not narrowed; the
  source genuinely has no data layer). The view still performs zero I/O.
- Shared components mapped: @/components/ui GlassPanel -> TSGlassPanel
  (apps/apple/Sources/Components/UI/Cards.swift; padding lg=16 == web p-4, glass material + border).
- `color` Tailwind class -> InfoTileValueColor enum on the shared semantic token palette
  (apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift), light/dark/high-contrast aware:
      text-[var(--text-primary)] (default) -> .primary  (Color.TS.textPrimary)
      text-[var(--text-muted)]             -> .muted    (Color.TS.textMuted)
      text-emerald-300                     -> .success  (Color.TS.statusSuccess)
      text-amber-300                       -> .warning  (Color.TS.statusWarning)
      text-rose-300                        -> .danger   (Color.TS.statusDanger)
      (+ .info / .accent for completeness). All call-site colors in TelemetryGrid.tsx covered.
- `value: string|number|boolean` -> InfoTileValue (.text/.number/.bool) with a pure, unit-tested
  `display(localize:)` reproducing the web ternary; whole numbers print without ".0" and with no
  grouping (parity with JS String(number)).
- Type roles: label text-xs -> Font.TS.caption(12); value text-lg font-semibold -> Font.TS.section(18,
  semibold); sub text-[10px] -> .system(size:10) (same idiom CommandTile uses for its sublabel).
- i18n (P1/S10): the web hardcodes "Yes"/"No"; those + the native "never blank" em dash are routed
  through the InfoTileStrings NSLocalizedString facade (table "InfoTile") so the Swift view holds NO
  English literals. Keys: infoTile.value.yes / infoTile.value.no / infoTile.value.empty. The
  label/value/sub are already localized by the parent (TelemetryGrid t(...)) and passed in verbatim.
- Accessibility: the web tile is a STATIC (non-interactive) display whose full value lives in the
  `title` attribute. Native = ONE VoiceOver element whose label combines label+value+sub (full,
  untruncated value spoken even though it visually truncates); decorative icon hidden;
  `.help(displayValue)` reproduces the web `title` hover tooltip on macOS; stable accessibilityIdentifier
  derived from the label. Dynamic Type via tokens; no animation so Reduce Motion is moot.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted once via InfoTileModel.start() with slug "InfoTile".

